[Event "QGD: 4.Bg5 (Tartakower)"]

{Black holds d5 with ...e6, castles, and frees the position with ...b6 and ...Bb7, or with ...c5.}
1. d4 {Takes the centre. The pawn on d4 controls c5 and e5. It also opens a line for the bishop on c1 and the queen on d1.}
1... d5 {Claims the centre: the pawn on d5 controls c4 and e4. It also opens a line for the bishop on c8 and the queen on d8.}
2. c4 {[%cal Gc4d5] The Queen's Gambit. Supports the centre: the pawn on c4 controls b5 and eyes the pawn on d5. It also opens a line for the queen on d1.}
2... e6 {[%cal Ge6d5] Declined. Black holds d5. Supports the centre: the pawn on e6 controls f5 and supports the pawn on d5. It also opens a line for the queen on d8 and the bishop on f8.}
3. Nc3 {Pressure on d5. Develops the knight to c3, where it controls e4 and eyes the pawn on d5.}
3... Nf6 {Develops the knight to f6, where it controls e4 and supports the pawn on d5.}
4. Bg5 {[%cal Gg5f6] Pins. Develops the bishop to g5, where it controls f4 and eyes the knight on f6. Black's last move put a knight on f6, which this now pressures.}
(4. Bf4 {Develops the bishop to f4, where it controls e5.}
 4... Be7 {Develops the bishop to e7, where it controls d6 and supports the knight on f6. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
 5. e3 {Supports the centre: the pawn on e3 supports the pawn on d4 and the bishop on f4. It also opens a line for the queen on d1 and the bishop on f1.}
 5... O-O {Castles kingside: the king is safe and the rook on f8 joins the game.}
 6. Nf3 {Develops the knight to f3, where it controls e5 and supports the pawn on d4.}
 6... c5 {Strikes at d4. Supports the centre: the pawn on c5 controls b4 and eyes the pawn on d4. It also opens a line for the queen on d8.}
 7. dxc5 {Takes the pawn on c5; Black will want to recapture.}
 7... Bxc5 {Recaptures on c5, restoring the material balance.})
4... Be7 {Breaks the pin. Develops the bishop to e7, where it controls d6 and supports the knight on f6. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
5. e3 {Supports the centre: the pawn on e3 controls f4 and supports the pawn on d4. It also opens a line for the queen on d1 and the bishop on f1.}
(5. Nf3 {Develops the knight to f3, where it controls e5 and supports the pawn on d4.}
 5... h6 {Questions the bishop. The pawn on h6 eyes the bishop on g5.}
 6. Bh4 {Keeps the pin. Moves the bishop out of attack to h4.}
 6... O-O {Castles kingside: the king is safe and the rook on f8 joins the game.}
 7. e3 {Supports the centre: the pawn on e3 controls f4 and supports the pawn on d4. It also opens a line for the bishop on f1.}
 7... b6 {The Tartakower. The pawn on b6 controls a5 and c5.})
5... O-O {Castles kingside: the king is safe and the rook on f8 joins the game.}
6. Nf3 {Develops the knight to f3, where it controls e5 and supports the pawn on d4.}
6... h6 {Questions the bishop. The pawn on h6 eyes the bishop on g5.}
7. Bh4 {Keeps the pin. Moves the bishop out of attack to h4.}
7... b6 {[%cal Gc8b7] The Tartakower. It prepares ...Bb7. The pawn on b6 controls a5 and c5.}
8. Be2 {Develops the bishop to e2, where it controls d3 and supports the knight on f3. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
8... Bb7 {Fianchettoes the bishop on b7, where it rakes the long diagonal through c6 and d5.}
9. Bxf6 {Takes the knight on f6; Black will want to recapture.}
9... Bxf6 {Recaptures on f6, restoring the material balance.}
10. cxd5 {Takes the pawn on d5; Black will want to recapture.}
10... exd5 {[%cal Gb7d5] Recaptures. The pawn on d5 is solid. Recaptures on d5, restoring the material balance.} *

[Event "QGD: Exchange"]

{In the Carlsbad structure, White often plays a minority attack with b4 and b5.}
1. d4 {Takes the centre. The pawn on d4 controls c5 and e5. It also opens a line for the bishop on c1 and the queen on d1.}
1... d5 {Claims the centre: the pawn on d5 controls c4 and e4. It also opens a line for the bishop on c8 and the queen on d8.}
2. c4 {The Queen's Gambit. Supports the centre: the pawn on c4 controls b5 and eyes the pawn on d5. It also opens a line for the queen on d1.}
2... e6 {Declined. Supports the centre: the pawn on e6 controls f5 and supports the pawn on d5. It also opens a line for the queen on d8 and the bishop on f8.}
3. Nc3 {Pressure on d5. Develops the knight to c3, where it controls e4 and eyes the pawn on d5.}
3... Nf6 {Develops the knight to f6, where it controls e4 and supports the pawn on d5.}
4. cxd5 {The Exchange. Takes the pawn on d5; Black will want to recapture.}
4... exd5 {[%cal Gc8f5] Recaptures, opening the bishop. Recaptures on d5, restoring the material balance.}
5. Bg5 {Pins. Develops the bishop to g5, where it controls f4 and eyes the knight on f6.}
5... c6 {Supports the centre: the pawn on c6 controls b5 and supports the pawn on d5. It also opens a line for the queen on d8.}
6. e3 {Supports the centre: the pawn on e3 controls f4 and supports the pawn on d4. It also opens a line for the queen on d1 and the bishop on f1.}
6... Be7 {Develops the bishop to e7, where it controls d6 and supports the knight on f6. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
7. Bd3 {Develops the bishop to d3, where it controls e4.}
7... Nbd7 {Develops the knight to d7, where it controls e5.}
8. Qc2 {[%cal Gc2h7] Aims at h7. The queen goes to c2.}
8... O-O {Castles kingside: the king is safe and the rook on f8 joins the game.}
9. Nge2 {Develops the knight to e2, where it supports the pawn on d4. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
9... Re8 {The rook goes to e8.} *

[Event "QGD: 3.Nf3 / Catalan"]

{The Catalan: the g2-bishop pressures the queenside. Black often takes on c4 and holds the pawn for a while.}
1. d4 {Takes the centre. The pawn on d4 controls c5 and e5. It also opens a line for the bishop on c1 and the queen on d1.}
1... d5 {Claims the centre: the pawn on d5 controls c4 and e4. It also opens a line for the bishop on c8 and the queen on d8.}
2. c4 {The Queen's Gambit. Supports the centre: the pawn on c4 controls b5 and eyes the pawn on d5. It also opens a line for the queen on d1.}
2... e6 {Declined. Supports the centre: the pawn on e6 controls f5 and supports the pawn on d5. It also opens a line for the queen on d8 and the bishop on f8.}
3. Nf3 {Develops the knight to f3, where it controls e5 and supports the pawn on d4.}
3... Nf6 {Develops the knight to f6, where it controls e4 and supports the pawn on d5.}
4. g3 {[%cal Gf1g2] The Catalan. The pawn on g3 controls f4 and h4.}
(4. Nc3 {Develops the knight to c3, where it controls e4 and eyes the pawn on d5.}
 4... Be7 {Develops the bishop to e7, where it controls d6 and supports the knight on f6. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
 5. Bf4 {Develops the bishop to f4, where it controls e5.}
 5... O-O {Castles kingside: the king is safe and the rook on f8 joins the game.}
 6. e3 {Supports the centre: the pawn on e3 supports the pawn on d4 and the bishop on f4. It also opens a line for the bishop on f1.}
 6... c5 {Strikes at d4. Supports the centre: the pawn on c5 controls b4 and eyes the pawn on d4. It also opens a line for the queen on d8.}
 7. dxc5 {Takes the pawn on c5; Black will want to recapture.}
 7... Bxc5 {Recaptures on c5, restoring the material balance.}
 8. Qc2 {The queen goes to c2 and controls e4.}
 8... Nc6 {Develops the knight to c6, where it controls d4 and e5.})
4... Be7 {Develops the bishop to e7, where it controls d6 and supports the knight on f6. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
5. Bg2 {Fianchetto. The bishop on g2 rakes the long diagonal through f3. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
5... O-O {Castles kingside: the king is safe and the rook on f8 joins the game.}
6. O-O {Castles kingside: the king is safe and the rook on f1 joins the game.}
6... dxc4 {Takes the pawn. Takes the pawn on c4, and it cannot be taken back at once.}
7. Qc2 {Prepares to regain c4. The queen goes to c2 and controls e4. It attacks the pawn on c4, which is undefended.}
7... a6 {Prepares ...b5. The pawn on a6 controls b5.}
8. Qxc4 {Regains the pawn. Takes the pawn on c4, and it cannot be taken back at once.}
8... b5 {Gains space with tempo. The pawn on b5 takes a4 and c4 away from the opponent. It attacks the queen on c4, which is undefended.}
9. Qc2 {Moves the queen out of attack to c2 and controls e4.}
9... Bb7 {[%cal Gb7g2] Contests the diagonal. Fianchettoes the bishop on b7, where it rakes the long diagonal through c6, d5 and e4.} *

[Event "QGD vs London"]

{Against the London, Black plays ...c5 and ...Nc6 to put pressure on d4 and b2.}
1. d4 {Takes the centre. The pawn on d4 controls c5 and e5. It also opens a line for the bishop on c1 and the queen on d1.}
1... d5 {Claims the centre: the pawn on d5 controls c4 and e4. It also opens a line for the bishop on c8 and the queen on d8.}
2. Bf4 {The London. Develops the bishop to f4, where it controls e5.}
2... Nf6 {Develops the knight to f6, where it controls e4 and supports the pawn on d5.}
3. e3 {Supports the centre: the pawn on e3 supports the pawn on d4 and the bishop on f4. It also opens a line for the queen on d1 and the bishop on f1.}
3... e6 {Supports the centre: the pawn on e6 controls f5 and supports the pawn on d5. It also opens a line for the bishop on f8.}
4. Nf3 {Develops the knight to f3, where it controls e5 and supports the pawn on d4.}
4... c5 {Strikes at d4. Supports the centre: the pawn on c5 controls b4 and eyes the pawn on d4. It also opens a line for the queen on d8.}
5. c3 {Holds d4. Supports the centre: the pawn on c3 controls b4 and supports the pawn on d4. It also opens a line for the queen on d1.}
5... Nc6 {Pressure on d4. Develops the knight to c6, where it controls e5 and eyes the pawn on d4.}
6. Nbd2 {Develops the knight to d2, where it controls e4.}
6... Bd6 {[%cal Gd6f4] Challenges the f4-bishop. Develops the bishop to d6, where it controls e5. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
7. Bg3 {Keeps it. Regroups the bishop to g3 and controls e5. Black's last move put a bishop on d6, which this now pressures.}
7... O-O {Castles kingside: the king is safe and the rook on f8 joins the game.} *

[Event "QGD: Elephant Trap"]

{The trap: after 4...Nbd7, 5.cxd5 exd5 6.Nxd5?? loses to 6...Nxd5! 7.Bxd8 Bb4+ 8.Qd2 Bxd2+ 9.Kxd2 Kxd8, and Black is a piece up.}
1. d4 {Takes the centre. The pawn on d4 controls c5 and e5. It also opens a line for the bishop on c1 and the queen on d1.} 1... d5 {Claims the centre: the pawn on d5 controls c4 and e4. It also opens a line for the bishop on c8 and the queen on d8.} 2. c4 {The Queen's Gambit. Supports the centre: the pawn on c4 controls b5 and eyes the pawn on d5. It also opens a line for the queen on d1.} 2... e6 {Declined. Supports the centre: the pawn on e6 controls f5 and supports the pawn on d5. It also opens a line for the queen on d8 and the bishop on f8.} 3. Nc3 {Pressure on d5. Develops the knight to c3, where it controls e4 and eyes the pawn on d5.} 3... Nf6 {Develops the knight to f6, where it controls e4 and supports the pawn on d5.} 4. Bg5 {Pins the knight. Develops the bishop to g5, where it controls f4 and eyes the knight on f6. Black's last move put a knight on f6, which this now pressures.} 4... Nbd7 {[%csl Gd8] Looks like it leaves d5 loose, but it sets the trap.}
5. cxd5 {Takes the pawn on d5; Black will want to recapture.}
5... exd5 {Recaptures on d5, restoring the material balance.}
6. Nxd5?? {[%cal Gd5f6] White grabs a pawn because the f6-knight is pinned... or so it seems.}
6... Nxd5! {[%cal Gd5d8] Gives up the queen! Recaptures on d5, restoring the material balance.}
7. Bxd8 {Takes the queen. Takes the queen on d8; Black will want to recapture.}
7... Bb4+ {[%cal Gb4e1] Check. Develops the bishop to b4, where it controls c5 and d6. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
8. Qd2 {The only move. The queen goes to d2 and supports the pawn on d4. Black's last move put a bishop on b4, which this now pressures.}
8... Bxd2+ {Takes the queen. Takes the queen on d2; White will want to recapture. It gives check.}
9. Kxd2 {Recaptures on d2, restoring the material balance.}
9... Kxd8 {Black is a piece up. Takes the bishop on d8, and it cannot be taken back at once.} *

[Event "QGD: 5.Bf4"]

{5.Bf4 is the modern main line. Black answers with the ...c5 break and active piece play.}
1. d4 {Claims the centre: the pawn on d4 controls c5 and e5. It also opens a line for the bishop on c1 and the queen on d1.}
1... d5 {Claims the centre: the pawn on d5 controls c4 and e4. It also opens a line for the bishop on c8 and the queen on d8.}
2. c4 {The Queen's Gambit. Supports the centre: the pawn on c4 controls b5 and eyes the pawn on d5. It also opens a line for the queen on d1.}
2... e6 {[%csl Gd5] The QGD: holds d5 solidly. Supports the centre: the pawn on e6 controls f5 and supports the pawn on d5. It also opens a line for the queen on d8 and the bishop on f8.}
3. Nc3 {Pressure on d5. Develops the knight to c3, where it controls e4 and eyes the pawn on d5.}
3... Nf6 {Defends d5 and develops. The knight on f6 controls e4 and supports the pawn on d5.}
4. Nf3 {Develops the knight to f3, where it controls e5 and supports the pawn on d4.}
4... Be7 {Flexible development, ready to castle. The bishop on e7 controls d6 and supports the knight on f6. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
5. Bf4 {[%cal Gf4c7] Develops the bishop outside the pawn chain, eyeing c7 and b8.}
5... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
6. e3 {Solid support for d4. Supports the centre: the pawn on e3 supports the pawn on d4 and the bishop on f4. It also opens a line for the bishop on f1.}
6... c5 {[%cal Gc5d4] The key freeing break: Black challenges White's centre before it settles.}
7. dxc5 {Takes, hoping to gain time on the bishop. Takes the pawn on c5; Black will want to recapture.}
7... Bxc5 {Recaptures; the bishop is active on c5. Recaptures on c5, restoring the material balance.}
8. Qc2 {Eyes h7 and prepares Rd1 or O-O-O. The queen goes to c2 and controls e4.}
8... Nc6 {Develops with pressure on d4 and e5. The knight on c6 controls d4 and e5.}
9. a3 {Prepares b4 to gain queenside space with tempo.}
9... Qa5 {[%cal Ga5c3] Pins the c3-knight and eyes a3; Black's pieces are fully active.} *
